+Version: `3.0.0`. Kind: `per_puzzle`. Pinned rule: `57674fc89a33`.
+
+The generator now honors exact total occupied-cell counts and feasible dimensions;
+rejects malformed or incompatible pins rather than silently changing them; and
+separates negative fixtures from the ordinary texture domain. The five positive
+branches are `plain`, `swap_pair`, `on_axis`, `dense`, and `same_pair`.
+
+Every three consecutive unoverridden draws with the same seed and difficulty
+include a collision and a center-row witness. Together they refute the seven
+executable rivals declared in the module. Every nine draws also retain at least
+three canonical-scale examples in **every** difficulty band. Other profiles keep
+wide, dense, multiple-collision, same-color-pair, and repeated-color support.
+
+This is a finite-rival curriculum guarantee, not universal identifiability or
+measured model accuracy. Explicit pins or downstream resampling may break the
+schedule guarantee; check assembled lessons when changing either.
+
+`workspace/` contains an independent Racket census and a reusable all-stage
+battery wrapper. `tests/` contains the contract and tool regressions. See
+`notes.md` for the retained strict-linter disagreement. Approval remains derived
+from the catalog and independently reviewed evidence; it has not been changed.
