 # Working notes: 0c023af8384a
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Review 2026-09-28 — review-27f8c31f6124f652
+
+Model: GPT-6 Astra Pro. Baseline `2.0.2` → proposed `3.0.0`. Canonical rule and
+base authority files unchanged. The incoming associated-notes file was empty;
+no unrecorded rationale is attributed to its author.
+
+### Semantic boundary
+
+For an input `g`, output cell `(r,c)` is `g[h-1-r][c] or g[r][c]` for ARC
+colors 0..9. Thus an occupied pair `(a,b)`, where both values are nonzero and
+unequal, becomes `(b,a)`. It does not become `(a,b)`, `(max(a,b),max(a,b))`,
+or the result of sequentially reading and overwriting a mutable board.
+
+All five canonical pairs agree with the unchanged Racket program, but none
+contains a conflicting mirror pair. Conflict handling is therefore a declared
+positive extension grounded in the existing program, not uniquely inferred
+from the demonstrations. `strict_canonical_like` excludes conflicts, while
+ordinary admission includes them. The original generator already sampled
+single collisions; this review fixes their lesson-level coverage rather than
+claiming to invent that feature.
+
+### Input contracts
+
+`marks` is the total occupied input count, including pair partners and center
+witnesses. Heights 4..16, widths 5..18, and marks 1..20 are global advertised
+bounds, not promises that every joint tuple is feasible. Pins stay exact.
+`on_axis` needs odd height and at least two marks; `swap_pair` needs two;
+`same_pair` needs three so it can retain a lone source and change the output.
+Orbit-capacity violations report the conflicting axes in a ValueError.
+Unknown keys and values fail loudly. Optional `None` values mean unpinned.
+
+Negative `empty_grid` and `already_symmetric` inputs remain available explicitly,
+but not in ordinary AXES.texture.valid, and self_check rejects their no-op
+outputs. Legal singletons, lines and blocks remain accepted when the rule
+changes them. Palette, rectangularity, sequence rows and dimensions are checked
+before applying the audit mirror.
+
+### Curriculum and coverage
+
+A seed-rotated cycle repeats:
+
+```
+plain, swap_pair, on_axis,
+same_pair, swap_pair, on_axis,
+dense, swap_pair, on_axis
+```
+
+Every three consecutive defaults contain one collision and one colored center
+row. An on-axis default has at least two lone sources; these refute pure-flip
+behavior. Collision witnesses refute destination-preserving, maximum, in-place,
+and one-direction-only rivals. Center witnesses refute axis erasure. This proves
+coverage for the declared seven competitors, not every possible program.
+
+Profiles 0,1,2 retain h=7..10, w=8..12, 3..4 distinct foreground marks in all
+bands; the other six retain broader difficulty-weighted support, repeated colors,
+and crowded/colliding cases. This repaired a real hard-band coverage regression
+found by the first all-stage post-change battery. No copied canonical board,
+battery-specific seed condition, opt-out or threshold change is used.
+
+### Measurements retained in the return
+
+- Named-rival ambiguity: 76/400 baseline lessons, 0/400 proposed lessons. Each
+  has three demonstrations and one query; four difficulty settings are sampled.
+- 5,907 distinct inputs evaluated by the canonical Racket rule, including all
+  1,100 two-cell/three-cell mirror-orbit color configurations and five canonical
+  pairs. Python audit expressions agree on the recorded cases.
+- Strict final battery: 11 green, 1 failed, all 12 stages run. Override matrix:
+  37,620 draws, 36,720 accepted and 900 structured incompatible-pin refusals.
+- Remaining failure: generic `selfcheck-minimal-impostor` warning promoted to
+  failure by strict defect_lint. Positive singleton/line/block outputs are
+  reference-checked in the probe; rejecting them would falsely narrow this task.
+
+The return includes earlier failures rather than replacing them with final
+logs. The two peer audits are findings-only; their sources were not edited.
+These measurements are generator/evaluation results, not trained-model scores.
